= Sexual and Gender Minorities

Unlike the old Penal Code of the dictatorship, the Republic's own 1932 Penal Code no longer criminalizes private homosexual acts between adults - a genuine, if quiet, liberalization. But that decriminalization is fragile: reformist doctors and jurists within the party warn that a new "vagrancy and danger" law being drafted by the Justice Ministry could be used to persecute homosexuals, cross-dressers, and other sexual minorities administratively, without ever needing to charge them with a crime.

- @repeal_1928_code: Formally strike the last provisions of the old Penal Code.
- @resist_vagrancy_law: Keep sexual minorities out of the new vagrancy law.
- @change_sex: Create a legal process for individuals to change their legal sex.
- @return: Do not enact any changes for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@repeal_1928_code
subtitle: Formally repeal what remains of the old dictatorship's Penal Code provisions criminalizing private acts.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have majority support for this policy.
view-if: repealed_1928_code == 0
choose-if: progressive_support >= 30
on-arrival: repealed_1928_code = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; ceda_relation -= 5; pce_relation += 4*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; catholic_psoe -= 4; economic_growth += 0.1;

Together with the <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> and left-leaning republicans, we have formally struck the last provisions of the old dictatorship's Penal Code that criminalized private acts between adults, entrenching the 1932 code's quiet liberalization against any future reversal.

Predictably, the CEDA and the far right accuse us of "degeneracy."

@resist_vagrancy_law
subtitle: Keep the incoming vagrancy law from being used against sexual minorities.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have majority support for this policy.
view-if: resisted_vagrancy_law == 0
choose-if: progressive_support >= 30
on-arrival: resisted_vagrancy_law = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; ceda_relation -= 5; pce_relation += 4*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; catholic_psoe -= 4; economic_growth += 0.1;

Voting together with the <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> and left-leaning republicans, we have amended the draft vagrancy law so that it cannot be turned against homosexuals, cross-dressers, and other sexual minorities as a matter of "social danger."


@change_sex
subtitle: We can create a legal process for individuals to change their legal sex, making their lives easier.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have majority support for this policy.
view-if: trans_rights == 0
choose-if: progressive_support >= 30
on-arrival: trans_rights = 1; homosexual_rights += 1; ceda_relation -= 5; pce_relation += 4*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front; catholic_psoe -= 4; economic_growth += 0.1;

We have passed a bill allowing legal recognition of transsexual and transvestite individuals in the sex in which they live, letting them change their legal name, dress as they wish without police persecution, and pursue medical treatment. It is a radical proposal for its time, championed by a handful of reformist doctors and jurists within the party.

Predictably, the CEDA and the far right accuse us of "degeneracy."
